  "arms_note": "`fused` is the shipped wider-group kernel (64 / head_size heads per workgroup), `narrow` is the one-workgroup-per-head kernel it replaced, `composed` is the two-dispatch chain and `default` is the route the decision record selects. `narrow_over_fused` and `composed_over_narrow` are what show whether widening the group moved the crossover instead of assuming it did, and the record is written from all three candidate timings.",
